    {
      "id": "d764594a-03a5-4d25-9ee3-5433a5379629",
      "type": "brief",
      "date": "2026-05-22T11:56:48.000Z",
      "title": "Full year 2026 earnings: Revenues exceed analysts expectations while EPS lags behind",
      "body": "Full year 2026 results: EPS: ₹12.86 (up from ₹11.78 in FY 2025). Revenue: ₹35.7b (up 12% from FY 2025). Net income: ₹578.2m (up 9.2% from FY 2025). Profit margin: 1.6% (down from 1.7% in FY 2025). Revenue exceeded analyst estimates by 1.8%. Earnings per share (EPS) missed analyst estimates by 48%. Revenue is forecast to grow 10% p.a. on average during the next 3 years, compared to a 12% growth forecast for the Machinery industry in India. Over the last 3 years on average, earnings per share has fallen by 51% per year but the company’s share price has only fallen by 18% per year, which means it has not declined as severely as earnings.",
      "keyDevTypeId": null,
      "source_url": null,
